      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the voiced alveolar fricative /z/, your vocal cords vibrate while air is forced past the tongue against the alveolar ridge to create turbulence. In contrast, for the unvoiced version /s/, your vocal cords remain apart and do not vibrate, meaning you produce the sound using only the airflow turbulence without vocal cord vibration. The primary technical distinction is simply that the period of phonation (voicing) is present in /z/ but absent in /s/.",
